# OASB is a security benchmark. The paths below are malicious-by-design test
# data and detection tooling, not application code. Scanning them produces
# expected findings (attack payloads, fake placeholder credentials, secret-
# detection regexes) that are the benchmark's purpose, not vulnerabilities.

# Benchmark corpus: labeled malicious + benign attack samples.
corpus/

# Secret-detection ruleset (contains regexes that match credential shapes).
.gitleaks.toml

# DVAA harness: connects to the intentionally-vulnerable DVAA agent endpoints.
src/harness/dvaa-manager.ts
src/harness/dvaa-client.ts
scripts/run-dvaa-benchmark.ts
